From 6d7f6bcc4ce96bdfc77b8492e0741facb0188118 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: AMB-1 FM6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:32:35 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] 1.3.99: reviewed for sharing: the reel read as it records,
 saved a sector a frame; its own identity

- the reel: a gene reading the block being recorded reads it as written so far and the rest as it was (its bytes past
  the head are of the coder's old state); a gene decodes afresh as it starts (what was recorded since is heard, no
  gene hears a reel erased)
- the reel saved a sector a UI frame (project_reel_step): the main loop between keeps the watchdog fed (8 s) and the
  screen shows how far it is; REC and EDIT wait for it
- the dice: SEL with a button that has no layer rolls nothing and keeps the undo
- AMB-1 FM6's own package identity (FM-1_76XXYYZZ), its repository, an unofficial fork's credits; the manual's install
  for this package; LICENSING: bank.c, reel.c, amb_syx.py, fm6_core.c's changes marked (Apache-2.0 4b), no DX7 voices

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
